From f778673ea7731eeb4c50faea6196f12d5cbd6496 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pierre-Hugues Husson <phh@phh.me>
Date: Tue, 7 May 2024 22:44:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Dont abort if the DnsHelper failed to init on BPF-less kernel

On BPF-less kernels (e.g. 4.14 on exynos7870) ADnsHelper_init() fails.
The upstream code aborts the whole resolv process, which brings down
netd/DnsResolver. For LOS-23.2/Android 16 the function now contains an
extra check for -EOPNOTSUPP on S/Sv2 before the LOG, so the old context
at line 690 no longer matches and `git am` fails with:

  error: DnsProxyListener.cpp:690
  Patch konnte nicht angewendet werden

Update the hunk to the current mainline context (3f8e973) at 698 and
replace abort() with return nullptr so the resolver gracefully
degrades (isUidNetworkingBlocked() returns false) instead of crashing.
Also makes the BPF-less 4.14 kernel usable on exynos7870-common.

Signed-off-by: Flominator <github.flominatorgd@gmail.com>
---
 DnsProxyListener.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/DnsProxyListener.cpp b/DnsProxyListener.cpp
index 3f8e973..ddc726b 100644
--- a/DnsProxyListener.cpp
+++ b/DnsProxyListener.cpp
@@ -698,7 +698,8 @@ IsUidBlockedFn resolveIsUidNetworkingBlockedFn() {
         // On S/Sv2 this can fail if tethering apex is too old, ignore it.
         if (ret == -EOPNOTSUPP && !isAtLeastT()) return nullptr;
         LOG(ERROR) << __func__ << ": ADnsHelper_init failed " << strerror(-ret);
-        abort();
+        // BPF-less kernel: don't abort, just degrade gracefully (exynos7870 4.14)
+        return nullptr;
     }
 
     // Related BPF maps were only mainlined from T.
